.TH ControlPanel 1 "February 2026"
.SH NAME
ControlPanel \- Configure desktop settings for FOX Toolkit applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBControlPanel\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
The ControlPanel allows the user to change the color themes, fonts, and file bindings of
FOX Toolkit based programs.

.SH USAGE
.LP
The ControlPanel has three tabs: \fBThemes\fP, \fBBindings\fP, and \fBGeneral\fP.

.br
The Themes tab is used to control color themes, individual colors, and the system
font.  Next to the built-in FOX color themes, it lists the GTK, KDE and FOX
themes installed in the usual desktop theme directories; choosing one imports
its colors and metrics with the theme importer and remembers the source so the
selection survives a restart.  The \fBImport...\fP button reads a gtk.css,
gtkrc, .colors or .foxtheme file directly, and \fBRescan\fP refreshes the list
after a theme was installed.  The \fBShow\fP filter narrows the list to
GNOME/GTK, KDE, built-in FOX presets, system-wide or per-user themes.
.br
The sampler is rendered with the selected theme itself, so it shows the theme's
colors, metrics, fonts and rounded control shapes.  A note at the bottom of the
window names the active theme source.

.br
The Bindings tab is used to associate file extension-associations with a description,
command, and mime-type.  The user can also assign icons.

.br
The General tab is used to control some common parameters of FOX Toolkit programs, such as
tooltip delay, mouse wheel speed, and so on.

